        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "3bca73c6-ef68-5931-b098-41fa042f1a1f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Films: Johnny Tremain, Song of the South\n- People: Walt Disney, Esther Forbes, Hal Stalmaster\n- Companies: Walt Disney Productions, WED Enterprises\n- Places: Boston, Massachusetts, Anaheim, California\n- Parks and Attractions: Magic Kingdom, Disneyland Park, Disneyland, Tokyo Disneyland, Walt Disney World Resort, Splash Mountain\n- Topics: American Revolution, fairy tales, Disney characters\n\nFacts:\n- Esther Forbes wrote the children's novel Johnny Tremain, which won the 1944 Newbery Medal.\n- Disney released Song of the South as a film in 1946.\n- Walt Disney Productions made Johnny Tremain in 1957, and the film retells the years in Boston, Massachusetts before the outbreak of the American Revolution.\n- Hal Stalmaster, born March 29, 1940, is an American former actor known for the lead role in the 1957 Walt Disney film Johnny Tremain.\n- Magic Kingdom was initialized by Walt Disney and designed by WED Enterprises, and its layout and attractions were based on Disneyland Park in Anaheim, California.\n- Magic Kingdom is dedicated to fairy tales and Disney characters.\n- Splash Mountain is a log flume dark ride located at Disneyland, Tokyo Disneyland, and the Magic Kingdom at the Walt Disney World Resort.\n- Splash Mountain is based on the characters, stories, and songs from the 1946 Disney film Song of the South.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "5a541974-c559-5afa-bbeb-042f90b9b569",
        "text": "Page: Johnny Tremain (film). Sentence: Johnny Tremain is a 1957 film made by Walt Disney Productions, based on the 1944 Newbery Medal-winning children's novel of the same name by Esther Forbes, retelling the story of the years in Boston, Massachusetts prior to the outbreak of the American Revolution.\nPage: Magic Kingdom. Sentence: Initialized by Walt Disney and designed by WED Enterprises, its layout and attractions are based on Disneyland Park in Anaheim, California, and is dedicated to fairy tales and Disney characters.\nPage: Hal Stalmaster. Sentence: Harry Lapidus Stalmaster, known as Hal Stalmaster (born March 29, 1940), is an American former actor, known for his lead role in the 1957 Walt Disney film of the American Revolution \"Johnny Tremain\", based on the 1943 Esther Forbes novel of the same name.\nPage: Splash Mountain. Sentence: Splash Mountain is a log flume dark ride at Disneyland, Tokyo Disneyland, and the Magic Kingdom at the Walt Disney World Resort, based on the characters, stories, and songs from the 1946 Disney film \"Song of the South\".",
